      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [27, 18, 28]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [27, 10, 28]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 21.78 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nAn analysis of the accessibility of each read and write operation mentioned in the defect report is as follows:\n\n1.  **Read of `myglobal` at line 27 in `svp_simple_505_001_main`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements (`if`, `while`, etc.).\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: The function `svp_simple_505_001_main` is the main entry point of the program. Execution will proceed sequentially, and this line will be executed.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is **reachable**.\n\n2.  **Write to `myglobal` at line 28 in `svp_simple_505_001_main`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: This line is executed sequentially after the read at line 27 within the `main` function.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is **reachable**.\n\n3.  **Write to `myglobal` at line 18 in `svp_simple_505_001_isr_1`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements within the ISR.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: The function `svp_simple_505_001_isr_1` is an interrupt service routine. Assuming interrupts are enabled (the code shows no calls to `disable_isr`), this ISR can preempt the `main` function. If preemption occurs after the read at line 27 and before the write at line 28 in `main`, the code inside this ISR, including the write at line 18, will be executed.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is **reachable**.\n\n4.  **Write to `myglobal` at line 10 in `isr_fun`**:\n    *   **Control Conditions**: This operation is not guarded by any control statements within the `isr_fun` function.\n    *   **Execution Analysis**: The function `isr_fun` is called by `svp_simple_505_001_isr_1` at line 20. As established above, the ISR `svp_simple_505_001_isr_1` is reachable. Therefore, its call to `isr_fun` is also reachable, and the write operation at line 10 will be executed.\n    *   **Conclusion**: This operation is **reachable**.\n\nAll read/write operations listed in the initial defect report are reachable. The code lacks any synchronization mechanisms, allowing the interrupt service routine `svp_simple_505_001_isr_1` to preempt the `main` function between its read and write operations on `myglobal`. This preemption can lead to the atomicity violations described. Therefore, the original report is correct.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"27\", \"18\", \"28\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"myglobal\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"27\", \"10\", \"28\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\nAbstain\n\n"
